    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0201" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/482</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Near
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-26">May 26, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I inquired of Mr. Hackworth<anchor n="1" xml:id="d95-f1"/> what bearing, if any,
                    in his opinion the bloodless <hi rendition="#italic">coup d’état</hi> in
                    Bulgaria of May 19, 1934, might have on the question of recognition. Mr.
                    Hackworth stated that he considered that the question of recognition did not
                    arise as there had been no change either in régime or in the head of the State;
                    while it was true that the cabinet change which resulted from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">coup d’état</hi> was brought about by means which were
                    non-parliamentary in character <pb facs="0202" n="102" xml:id="pg102"/> the
                    important element to be considered in this connection was that the King had
                    immediately, by official decree, given his sanction to the change.</p>
                <p>The foregoing views expressed by Mr. Hackworth confirm in every respect my own
                    conclusions in the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="1" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Green H. Hackworth, Legal Adviser.</p>
